From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: novadeck <novadeck@localhost>
Date: Sun, 7 Sep 2026 19:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Battery: find the pack by supply TYPE, not by name

Upstream matches "BAT" in the power-supply directory name, which is x86 firmware
naming. No board we ship uses it:

  SM8250            /sys/class/power_supply/battery          (pm8150b fuel gauge)
  SM8550/8650/8750  /sys/class/power_supply/qcom-battmgr-bat (PMIC GLINK battmgr)

The previous novadeck patch hardcoded the first of those, so on every SM8550 and
SM8650 board -- i.e. most of the fleet -- the HUD found no battery at all and the
battery and power fields were blank. Measured on a KONKR Pocket FIT (SM8650).

Match POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_TYPE == "Battery" instead, which is what the kernel
guarantees and what both names resolve to, and skip scope=Device so a wireless
controllers own pack cannot be mistaken for the system battery -- something the
BAT* match used to exclude by accident. battPath holds two entries, so the loop
now stops at two rather than writing past the end.
---
--- a/src/battery.cpp
+++ b/src/battery.cpp
@@ -7,16 +7,32 @@
 
 void BatteryStats::numBattery() {
     int batteryCount = 0;
-    if (!fs::exists("/sys/class/power_supply/")) {
-         batteryCount = 0;
-    }
+    const int battMax = sizeof(battPath) / sizeof(battPath[0]);
     fs::path path("/sys/class/power_supply/");
+    if (!fs::exists(path)) {
+        batt_count = 0;
+        batt_check = true;
+        return;
+    }
     for (auto& p : fs::directory_iterator(path)) {
-        string fileName = p.path().filename();
-        if (fileName.find("BAT") != std::string::npos) {
-            battPath[batteryCount] = p.path();
-            batteryCount += 1;
-        }
+        if (batteryCount >= battMax)
+            break;
+        // Match on the supply's TYPE rather than its name. Only x86 firmware calls the pack
+        // BAT*: a Qualcomm handheld exposes "battery" (pm8150b fuel gauge, SM8250) or
+        // "qcom-battmgr-bat" (PMIC GLINK, SM8550/SM8650/SM8750), and the same directory holds
+        // the charger and wireless supplies, which are not batteries at all.
+        string type;
+        std::ifstream type_input(p.path() / "type");
+        if (!getline(type_input, type) || type.compare(0, 7, "Battery") != 0)
+            continue;
+        // scope=Device is a peripheral's pack -- a wireless controller, a stylus -- not the
+        // system battery. Matching BAT* excluded those by accident; matching the type does not.
+        string scope;
+        std::ifstream scope_input(p.path() / "scope");
+        if (getline(scope_input, scope) && scope.compare(0, 6, "Device") == 0)
+            continue;
+        battPath[batteryCount] = p.path();
+        batteryCount += 1;
     }
     batt_count = batteryCount;
     batt_check = true;
-- 
